    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/121-South-Main-Street/Grants-and-Financial-Specialist_REQ211099": {
      "title": "Grants and Financial Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Grants and Financial Specialist independently manages all matters pertaining to grants administration, both financial and administrative, and has financial oversight and administrative responsibility for the sponsored projects. This position provides high-level comprehensive pre- and post- award management, subcontract administration, and financial analysis. This position is the administrative liaison between the administrative core, the Office of Sponsored Projects (OSP), collaborating institutions, sponsoring agencies, and principal investigators (PIs). The incumbent has a broad scope and knowledge of research administration and financial matters. This position is hybrid eligible, with the expectation of three days in the office. Workload can be unpredictable with hard deadlines. Successful incumbent will have the ability and willingness to work outside of the normal business hours on occasion in order to comply with OSP and sponsor driven deadlines. All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification that are satisfactory to Brown University. Job Competencies: ● Excellent financial analytical ability. ● Knowledge of OMB circulars is preferred. ● Willingness and interest in assuming increasing levels of responsibilities, networking, leadership, and training opportunities. ● Highly proficient in Excel applications (data manipulations); MS Excel and Google Docs preferred. ● Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to work independently. ● Excellent communication skills (both oral and written) to elicit and disperse information; to present information (including data) and communications in a clear and concise manner. ● Strong organizational, administrative, time management and critical thinking skills. ● Ability to analyze and reconcile accounts. ● Ability to meet deadlines in a fast-paced, multi-faceted work environment. ● Ability to organize and prioritize workload in a multi-tasking environment while maintaining careful attention to detail. Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree required. A degree in Accounting, Finance or related fields is preferred. Experience: At least 2-4 years of experience in research administration or accounting/financial/budgeting experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience with proposal preparation with federal and non-federal grants and using InfoEd/Coeus grants management (or similar) system. Familiarity with eRA Commons, NSF Fastlane, Research.gov and/or Grants.gov preferred. Higher-Education or non-profit work experience preferred, or equivalent combination of education/experience. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-26 Job Posting Title: Grants and Financial Specialist Department: School of Public Health Office of Finance and Administration Grade: Grade 9 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/225-Dyer-Street/Associate-Director--Marketing-Program-Management_REQ211016": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Marketing Program Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: About Brown: Brown University is a leading research university distinct for its student-centered learning and deep sense of purpose. Our students, faculty and staff are driven by the idea that their work will have an impact in the world. Brown University offers a flexible work/life balance; summer hours, winter break and a comprehensive Benefits package including time off, annual paid holidays; benefits offerings including health, dental, vision, tuition assistance, retirement, wellness, employee discounts and more. To learn about Brown University’s benefits, visit the University Human Resources web page for further information.  About the Opportunity: Brown University’s School of Professional Studies (SPS) brings a Brown education to new audiences of learners: those focused on the development of skills and a breadth of knowledge necessary for professional success and leadership. We leverage Brown’s intellectual centers of excellence, rigorous teaching, and developmental approach to learning in a range of programs, including serving students outside of traditional degree programs. We partner with Brown departments, centers, institutes, and schools to develop degree and non-degree programs, and to support the recruitment, retention, and placement success of master’s students, including traditional, non-traditional, and professional students. Responsibilities:   The School of Professional Studies (SPS) at Brown University seeks an Associate Director, Marketing Program Management to provide operational leadership for the planning, prioritization and execution of the School's marketing initiatives.  Reporting to the Director of Marketing and Communications, this role serves as the primary relationship manager between SPS Marketing and Communications and academic and administrative partners across the university.The position leads project planning, prioritization and cross-functional coordination for a complex portfolio of marketing initiatives, supporting over 40 master’s, professional and executive education programs.  Working collaboratively across departments, the Associate Director advises stakeholders on project scope, timelines and resource planning while developing scalable operational processes, identifying workflow bottlenecks and leading continuous improvement initiatives that strengthen departmental effectiveness. As the team evolves, this role may also provide day-to-day oversight, coaching and performance management for one to two direct reports.   Qualifications:   Required Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, business, project management or related field, or equivalent combination of education and experience Minimum 5-7 years of experience in project management, account management, client services or marketing operations Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, including experience preparing reports and presenting  Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships and advise stakeholders in a complex organizational environment. Experience utilizing project management systems such as ClickUp, Asana, Monday.com, or similar platforms Strong organizational, analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to develop operational improvements. Ability to prioritize  competing initiatives, resources and adapt to changing priorities Experience synthesizing data and project information into reports and recommendations that support leadership decision-making. Preferred   Experience working at a marketing agency, client services or project management environment strongly preferred Experience in higher education marketing, communications or creative operations Familiarity with marketing and creative production workflows 1-2 years of supervisory experience preferred Experience coordinating integrated marketing initiatives across multiple channels Familiarity with accessibility considerations for digital content and communications   Salary Grade: 11 Additional Information:  Applicants are asked to include a resume and cover letter. Must be available to work during the Master’s Commencement Ceremony, which falls on Memorial Day weekend. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check.     Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-21 Job Posting Title: Associate Director, Marketing Program Management Department: School of Professional Studies and Masters Programs Grade: Grade 11 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Sternlicht-Commons/Medical-Assistant_REQ211106": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Medical Assistant is an integral part of the health care team at Health Services that serves the diverse student population at Brown.  The MA is responsible for the intake and preparation of patients, assisting medical providers, performing waived tests, stocking, cleaning (per infection control protocols), scheduling appointments(internal/external), and performing office duties including release of information, faxing, scanning, copying, filing, referrals and referral tracking. Job Qualifications  Education and Experience Certification from a Medical Assistant training program or equivalent including training in medical and office assisting. High School Diploma or GED required. Clinical experience in an ambulatory setting. CPR certification. Minimum one-year medical office experience preferred. Job Competencies Excellent communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to provide culturally competent care to a diverse population required; experience working with diverse student populations preferred. Demonstrated ability and willingness to work in and support a diverse and inclusive environment. Orientation towards quality customer service necessary. Computer efficiency and experience with EHR preferred. Background Check:  All offers of employment are contingent upon a successful criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown. Additional Information : Please submit a resume and cover letter when applying for this position. To learn about benefits at Brown University, visit the  Brown University benefits  page. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-26 Job Posting Title: Medical Assistant Department: Health Services Grade: Grade 6 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Onsite   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Maddock-Alumni-Center/Program-Associate--Alumni-Belonging_REQ211114": {
      "title": "Program Associate, Alumni Belonging",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Program Associate provides operational, administrative, and programmatic support for the Alumni Belonging team and its portfolio of affinity group communities, shared interest groups, and community and belonging initiatives. The Associate supports the day-to-day operations of Alumni Belonging programs, including Affinity Groups, Shared Interest Groups, and matriculation campaigns. Program support responsibilities include maintaining and updating the online BrownConnect+ platform, assisting in the coordination of virtual and in-person events, and contributing to the production of invitations, newsletters, and other external communications. A key focus of this role is budget administration. The Associate maintains and updates budget-tracking documents, supports the annual reconciliation process for all affinity and shared-interest group budgets, creates treasury summary statements, and submits funding requests and reimbursement requests in a timely manner. The Associate also supports data tracking and annual metrics reporting, including volunteer coding and event registration processes, administering constituent surveys, compiling data from multiple sources, and assisting staff in producing annual program reports that track progress against goals and identify opportunities for improvement and innovation. This position collaborates with colleagues across Alumni Relations, Advancement, and other University partners, and provides direct customer service to alumni, students, family members, and University colleagues The Alumni Belonging Pillar builds and supports an ecosystem of communities based on affinity and shared interests that speak to the multiplicity and intersectionality of the alumni community's lived experiences, interests, and needs. The team nurtures and grows a culture of belonging for alumni and their parents, family, and friends by promoting diversity and inclusion across all alumni engagement programming. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of 2 years of experience in a related field such as alumni relations, fundraising, higher education, administrative support, volunteer management, and/or community building. Experience with event planning preferred. Job Competencies Excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent attention to detail and excellent organizational skills, interpersonal skills, and project and time management skills. Expertise in Microsoft and Google platforms, especially Google Calendar and email, Google Docs, Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint Proficient with audio/visual and presentation platforms (Zoom, Microsoft Teams or WebEx, PowerPoint, etc.) Excellent attention to detail and excellent organizational skills, interpersonal skills, and project and time management skills. Familiarity with financial and operational systems and processes. Proven ability to analyze data, research information, problem-solve, and coordinate projects. Ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities in a fast-paced, multi-faceted work environment with emphasis on accuracy and deadline adherence. Ability to effectively and efficiently multitask and prioritize workload. Willingness and ability to support a diverse and inclusive campus community. Ability to apply tact and maintain confidentiality. Customer-focused, customer service orientation. Ability to work occasional nights and weekends as needed. Willingness and ability to occasionally work a non-traditional schedule as needed (i.e., weekend or evening events, etc.). Preferred Qualifications Experience using AI-powered tools to support proposal writing, build presentations, and administrative workflows. Comfort and facility with digital platforms and the ability to quickly learn new tools; prior experience with online community or event management platforms is a plus. Background Check: All offers of employment are contingent upon a successful criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown. Additional Information: Please submit a resume and cover letter when applying for this position. Read more about the benefits of working at Brown here . Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-27 Job Posting Title: Program Associate, Alumni Belonging Department: Alumni Relations Grade: Grade 8 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/55-Claverick-Street/Research-Assistant_REQ210937": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The primary purpose of this position is to conduct vaccine development studies for Plasmodium falciparum. Under the supervision of the Principal Investigator, the Research Assistant will assist with maintaining malaria parasites and bacterial cultures, limited pilot scale protein production, protein purification with fast performance liquid chromatography, western blots and other basic microbiology benchtop techniques. The Research Assistant will assist with performing animal immunizations and collection of vaccine anti-sera. The Research Assistant will be responsible for keeping supplies in stock, and will provide technical support for the research project. The Kurtis lab’s research focuses on understanding the mechanisms that cause tropical diseases such as Malaria. Experiments performed include western blot, PCR assays, parasite assays, and ELISA based assays. This is a fixed term position with a current end date of 9/30/2027 which may be extended based upon available funding. Education and Experience Required: B.S. or B.A. in Biology-related field. Required: Prior related research experience or extensive coursework in molecular biology, parasitology and immunology And/or equivalent combination of education and experience. General background knowledge of malaria parasite biology is a plus Job Competencies Ability to be organized and productive Ability to communicate clearly and professionally Ability to keep accurate records Ability to follow detailed instructions Proficiency with computers and essential software programs (such as MS office) Willingness and ability to occasionally work evenings and/or weekends for parasite culture maintenance The person in this position frequently communicates to faculty and staff who inquire about their research. Must be able to exchange accurate information. CRMINAL BACKGROUND AND EDUCATION CHECK REQUIRED Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-18 Job Posting Title: Research Assistant Department: Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine Grade: Grade 7 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Fixed Term (Fixed Term) Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Onsite   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Barus--Holley/Research-Assistant_REQ211120": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The School of Engineering at Brown University has a new and exciting opportunity to hire a Research Assistant. The Research assistant will support the Health Innovation Technology Sandbox (HITS) in the Brown University School of Engineering.   The incumbent will work on the design, fabrication, and testing of wearable health monitoring sensors, including those using photoplethysmography (PPG), kinematic sensors, and AI enhanced sensors. Daily tasks include:  performing optical experiments, electronics development, signal processing, data analysis, presenting results regularly at lab meetings and working jointly with other lab members on development of an equitable pulse oximeter. Position will also assist with on-going clinical studies.    This is a full-time, fixed term position for one year, but is eligible for extension with secured external funding. Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The successful candidate, as a minimum, should have the following background:  Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering and one to two years’ experience or equivalent combination of education and experience, required. Experience gained as an undergraduate working in an optics lab is highly preferred. Job Competencies Excellent communication skills, written and verbal with a professional demeanor in all communications, including but not limited to emails, reports, meetings and presentations. The candidate must produce quality work that prioritizes accuracy and thoroughness. Treats co-workers with respect, honesty, and fairness. Resolves issues effectively and is viewed as a positive team member and/or colleague. Ability to work independently and implement short- and long-term goals independently, but also as a strong team member when the situation warrants. Demonstrated mastery of MS/Office, matlab Demonstrated ability to support a community of diverse perspectives and cultures in an inclusive environment.  Incumbent must be highly professional and able to interact successfully with individuals at all levels. Travel may be required for assisting in field research. Occasional presentations of research findings to internal and external collaborators may be required. Please submit a cover letter, specifying which position you are applying to and a resume with your application. All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown University. For current information on Brown's vaccine requirements and other community health matters, please refer to the Healthy Brown website. Why Brown? Brown University is a leading research university that is distinct for its student-centered learning and deep sense of purpose. Our students, faculty, and staff are driven by the idea that their work will impact the world. Brown University offers a flexible work/life balance, summer hours, winter break, and a comprehensive Benefits package, including time off and annual paid holidays. Benefit offerings include health, dental, vision, tuition assistance, retirement, wellness, employee discounts, and more.  Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-27 Job Posting Title: Research Assistant Department: School of Engineering Grade: Grade 8 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Fixed Term (Fixed Term) Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Onsite   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/South-Street-Landing/Program-Coordinator_REQ211019": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Department of Public Safety and Emergency Management’s (DPSEM) Program Coordinator provides operational and programmatic support for community engagement and outreach initiatives. This individual plays a key role in coordinating and implementing community-building initiatives among students, staff, and community members that promote a deepening sense of belonging, trust, and connection with the department. In carrying out these responsibilities, this individual works to improve community empowerment, community-police relations, transparency, and accountability. The Coordinator supports the Director of Advocacy, Engagement, and Communications by organizing events and programs, managing outreach and communications, and carrying out day-to-day administrative tasks. Major Responsibility:  Facilitate programming and advocacy initiatives: Coordinate and implement DPS events and programs, including the MET High School internship program, etc. Carry a portfolio of managing at least two programs/events that engage with the student population Provide logistical support in coordinating meetings, managing the department engagement calendar, as well as logistics for programs (taking meeting minutes, event set-up, food, location, securing guest speakers, emailing and posting flyers around campus, and photography)Conduct outreach and identify student groups and departments for future partnerships Support the development of opportunities for partnerships by engaging community organizations, community leaders, youth, and other stakeholders in Providence. Supervise student assistants and manage assignments that support department success, such as distribution of printed and electronic materials; other clerical needs; general event supportRepresent the team at events and programs, with a willingness to train and serve as an instructor for courses  Research different topics of importance, such as policing, community relations, accountability, safety, and resources for survivors of crime Attend and participate in on and off-campus working groups Major Responsibility:  Support the department’s communications efforts: Assist the Director with communications projects as needed Draft the community newsletter, including gathering content and growing audiences Manage department social media accounts Assist with the design of graphic materials, including event posters, recruitment materials, safety information, maps, and pamphlets Maintain website updates Support public information and transparency initiatives, including the DPS Community Survey, complaint forms, and other feedback mechanisms Create PowerPoints and other tools for presentations Major Responsibility: Data Collection and Dissemination: Manage the registration system and track attendance metrics for department events, programs, and training courses. Maintain and audit the monthly inventory of department materials, outreach supplies, and promotional items Monitor, analyze, and report on social media and website analytics to evaluate the reach and effectiveness of digital communication strategies Assist with implementing digital and in-person strategies to collect feedback, recommendations, and input from community members Assist with gathering and collecting data for annual reporting and CALEA accreditation Decisions free to make: Responding to inquiries regarding programs and concerns from community members Manage and adjust the program calendar, schedule routine meetings, and coordinate logistics for events or workshops Resolve minor, day-to-day concerns with program participants, vendors, or venues using established procedures Decisions that depend on position’s advice: Making modifications to program curriculum, eligibility criteria, project timelines, etc. Issuing public-facing materials and communications Budget expenditures Dimensions: Engagement and programming for the University’s approximately 10,000 students and 4,000 staff/faculty regarding personal and public safety issues. Working with the Director, publicize department events and programs creating and utilizing a variety of marketing tools Working with staff and faculty to create and maintain relationships with University/community partners and area organizations and provide coordination for partnership programming Working with staff and students, initiate meetings and manage logistics; execute communications to involved parties Supervise student assistants and manage assignments that support department success such as distribution of printed and electronic materials; other clerical needs; general event support Use practical and mature judgment to resolve low to medium level conflicts or issues as they arise Job Qualifications and Competencies: Education and Experience: Bachelor’s Degree preferred, plus 2- 3 years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge of higher-education or non-profit setting is highly desirable. Job Competencies: Strong project management, organizational skills, and event planning experience Keen attention to detail Must have the ability to think critically and creatively Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate, collaborate, and connect with people with various backgrounds, identities, and lived experiences. Strong listening, oral, and written communication skills. Computer skills/experience in: Microsoft Office Suite, Google Suite, and Social Media.platforms Must be flexible and able to adapt in a changing and emergency -service centered environment and able to meet time-sensitive deadlines. Understanding and familiarity of issues regarding policing and groups from diverse populations, particularly from BIPOC, LGBTQ+, undocumented, first-generation college, low-income, and international communities Experience in outreach, marketing, or grassroots/community organizing Familiarity with programs like Canva, Adobe, Qualtricsor Mailchimp a plus. Evenings, weekends, and holidays may occasionally be required. All offers are contingent on the successful completion of a criminal background check and education verification. All offers of employment are contingent upon consent to criminal background screening and education verification with results satisfactory to Brown Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-24 Job Posting Title: Program Coordinator Department: Public Safety and Emergency Management Grade: Grade 8 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/222-Richmond-Street/Accessibility-and-Learning-Specialist_REQ211160": {
      "title": "Accessibility and Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: SUMMARY: The Accessibility and Learning Specialist is a member of the Office of Academic Support, which is housed in the Office of Medical School Student Affairs at The Warren Alpert Medical School (the Medical School). The Office of Medical School Student Affairs supports medical students throughout medical school, in part by fostering an open, caring, and inclusive learning environment and serving as a responsive resource for medical students. In addition to medical students, students in the Program in Liberal Medical Education and students in Masters’ Degree Program that fall under the medical school umbrella (the Gateways in Medicine program) are also supported in their academic achievement. The Specialist conducts student intake interviews and reviews medical, psychological, and neuropsychological information to determine eligibility for accommodations and identifies what accommodations are appropriate based on the disability and program requirements. They support the Medical School, and its clinical partners in implementing those accommodations. In addition, the Specialist provides referrals to neuropsychological testing and to other clinicians as indicated. The Specialist also promotes student achievement by improving student academic skills through one-on-one learning consultations as well as group presentations.  The Specialist engages in professional development and other projects/activities as needed to support the Office of Academic Support. QUALIFICATIONS: Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in Counseling, Social Work, Higher Education, Rehabilitation Services or similar program plus 5-7 years of experience working with students with disabilities in a college setting Masters preferred. Counseling coursework preferred. Experience: or equivalent combination of education and experience. Formal training and education in disabilities services Experience working with diverse student populations Knowledge of ADA and of various learning disabilities Experience with reviewing and evaluating documentation to determine accommodations in higher education or employment settings. Job Competencies Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Thorough understanding of varied neuropsychological tests and their meaning Previous experience in similar role preferred High degree of discretion Strong attention to detail and organization Knowledge and understanding of ADA regulations, guidelines, and standards as applicable to a higher education or academic program. Effective problem solving and conflict resolution skills. Ability to manage multiple tasks and competing demands. Ability to work effectively as part of a team. Criminal Background and Education Check Required Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-28 Job Posting Title: Accessibility and Learning Specialist Department: Warren Alpert Medical School Grade: Grade 10 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/South-Street-Landing/Data-Curator_REQ211147": {
      "title": "Data Curator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: Data Curator Office of Information Technology Are you passionate about empowering campus partners and driving discovery through efficient data infrastructure? The Data Curator serves as a vital bridge between university researchers, administrative units, and central IT infrastructure. In this role, you will work directly with faculty, postdocs, staff, and leadership to support the research, academic, and administrative community in managing, protecting, and optimizing their data assets throughout the entire data lifecycle. Key Responsibilities Community Collaboration:   Partner directly with the research, academic, and administrative community to understand their unique storage challenges, providing consultative guidance on optimal storage placement and data management best practices. Data Lifecycle Management & Efficiency:   Proactively assist users with identifying obsolete or unused data for archiving, compression, or deletion—optimizing institutional storage space and keeping central infrastructure sustainable. Platform & Service Curation:   Lead organization and cleanup efforts across central cloud platforms (such as Google Workspace) and enterprise storage solutions. Institutional Advocacy:   Promote data hygiene, file organization conventions, and lifecycle workflows across all campus departments and research labs. Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree preferred. 5–7 years of hands-on experience in research IT support, data curation, academic technology, or enterprise storage lifecycle management. Required Knowledge, Skills, & Competencies Customer Collaboration:   Exceptional interpersonal and consultation skills, with a proven track record of building trust and partnering effectively with faculty, research labs, and administrative staff. Data Efficiency & Hygiene:   Strong   knowledge of data management best practices, including compression tools, file packaging ( tar ,   zip ), file system conventions, and storage tiering. Platform Familiarity:   Direct experience with central cloud storage services (Google Workspace) and enterprise storage environments (NAS, Object Storage, A rchival systems). System Administration Knowledge:   Previous experience managing Unix and Windows environments. Problem Solving:   Ability to translate complex user storage challenges into streamlined lifecycle and curation workflows. Regulatory Awareness:   Basic understanding of federal grant data mandates and data privacy/compliance frameworks (e.g., HIPAA, PII, PCI). Work Schedule & After-Hours Expectations Planned After-Hours Effort:   This role supports planned maintenance for services and routine scheduled events outside standard business hours. Mission-Critical Projects & Incidents:   Participation is required for large-scale planned or unplanned major incidents, which may occasionally require extended working hours outside business hours, including weekends or holidays. All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown University. In addition CJIS background check is required. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-28 Job Posting Title: Data Curator Department: Office of Information Technology Grade: Grade 11 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/75-Charlesfield-Street/Manager-of-Campus-Physical-Security_REQ211071": {
      "title": "Manager of Campus Physical Security",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Manager of Campus Physical Security serves as the university's subject matter expert on the physical security of campus buildings and grounds, including access control, video surveillance, intrusion detection, and related door and perimeter hardware. This role evaluates existing facilities and new construction and renovation projects against the university's established physical security standards, verifies and ensures ongoing compliance with those standards, contributes to their assessment and refinement, and serves as a standing member of the team that evaluates and vets incoming requests for new or modified security measures across campus.   This position reports to the Vice President for Public Safety and Emergency Management and works in close, ongoing partnership with the Public Safety technology teams (Office of Information Technology/OIT), as well as with Facilities and Campus Operations, to ensure that physical security decisions are coordinated across systems, construction, and day-to-day building operations. Major Responsibility: Facility Assessments and Standards Evaluation Conduct routine physical security assessments of existing campus buildings, evaluating access control, video surveillance coverage, intrusion detection, door hardware, lighting, and perimeter security against the university's established physical security standards. Apply CPTED (Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design) and ASIS International guidelines when assessing facility risk and vulnerability. Document assessment findings and produce reports with prioritized, actionable recommendations for remediation. Evaluate new construction and renovation plans against the university's established physical security standards, applying the existing baselines to design and specification reviews. Verify that facilities, system installations, and vendor work comply with the university's established physical security standards, and flag and track non-compliance items through remediation. Continually assess the university's physical security standards themselves, not just compliance with them, identifying gaps, outdated requirements, or emerging risks, and recommending updates through the appropriate governance process. Major Responsibility: Crime Prevention Through Environmental Design (CPTED) and Site Safety Assess campus lighting levels, fixture placement, and maintenance to support natural surveillance and reduce concealment areas along pathways, parking areas, and building exteriors. Evaluate landscaping, vegetation, and sightlines for blind spots and overgrowth that compromise visibility, and coordinate trimming or design changes with Facilities and Campus Operations. Review pedestrian pathways, parking layouts, and building entrances for natural access control, wayfinding, and territorial reinforcement (signage, landscaping edges, and other cues that distinguish public from private space). Evaluate the placement, coverage, and functionality of emergency blue-light phones, callboxes, and other emergency communication infrastructure across campus. Incorporate lighting, landscaping, sightline, and other safety-through-design factors into new construction and renovation reviews alongside access control and surveillance requirements Major Responsibility: Cross-Functional Coordination Partner closely with the OIT’s Public Safety Apps team on the technical implementation of access control, video management, and alarm systems, ensuring physical assessments and system configuration stay aligned. Coordinate with Facilities and Campus Operations on building conditions, maintenance schedules, construction or renovation timelines, and day-to-day building use, event scheduling, and occupancy patterns that affect physical security infrastructure. Attend design and construction meetings for capital projects to represent physical security standards and flag issues early in the design process. Perform field inspections during construction and at final commissioning to confirm security hardware is installed to specification. Major Responsibility: Security Request Evaluation Serve as a standing member of the team that reviews and evaluates incoming departmental requests for new or modified security measures (e.g., additional cameras, card readers, door hardware). Assess each request against the university's established security standards and risk criteria to determine need, appropriate placement, and hardware requirements. Provide recommendations and consult with requesting departments on scope, feasibility, and sequencing of approved work. Major Responsibility: Continuous Improvement Monitor the effectiveness of implemented security measures and standards, and recommend refinements as part of an ongoing, continuous review process; this role is expected to actively help evolve the university's physical security standards, not simply verify adherence to them. Track industry trends, emerging threats, and best practices, and bring recommended updates to standards forward through the appropriate governance channels. Contribute to after-action reviews following incidents or drills that touch physical security infrastructure. Decisions free to make: Set day-to-day priorities for projects, troubleshooting and break-fix of all University related security and safety systems. Budget input and oversight on project spending Identify areas of weaknesses that need to be addressed Verify that facilities, system installations, and vendor work comply with the university's established physical security standards, and flag and track non-compliance items through remediation. Decisions that depend on position’s advice: Primary owner of the hardware and software needed to provide a safe and secure operations that must have the ability to exert influence and set priority across a wide variety of departments including DSPEM, OIT, Facilities Management, and Executive Leadership. Serve as a standing member of the team that reviews and evaluates incoming departmental requests for new or modified security measures (e.g., additional cameras, card readers, door hardware). Document assessment findings and produce reports with prioritized, actionable recommendations for remediation. Dimensions: Reports directly to the Vice President for Public Safety and Emergency Management Effectively communicate and coordinate with University Facilities and Campus Operations regarding the coordination on construction, renovation, building maintenance, and day-to-day operational impacts affecting security infrastructure. Qualifications : Education and Experience 8+ years of experience in physical security assessment, physical security system design, or facilities/campus security oversight. Bachelor’s degree (preferred) Required Working knowledge of access control and video management systems (e.g., C·CURE, Genetec, etc) and standard door/lock hardware. Demonstrated ability to read architectural and low-voltage plans and translate them into security-relevant feedback. Strong collaboration and communication skills; proven ability to work effectively across public safety, IT, facilities, and operations teams. Preferred PSP (Physical Security Professional) certification from ASIS International. CPTED certification (Basic or Advanced). Experience in a higher education or large multi-building campus environment. Please include a cover letter when submitting your resume to the application. Criminal and education background check satisfactory to Brown University. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-25 Job Posting Title: Manager of Campus Physical Security Department: Public Safety and Emergency Management Grade: Grade 11 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Onsite   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/RT---Rhode-Island/Senior--Lead-Application-Administrator--Departmental-Systems_REQ211130": {
      "title": "Senior /Lead Application Administrator, Departmental Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: Senior /Lead Application Administrator, Departmental Systems Office of Information Technology The Office of Information Technology (OIT) is seeking a skilled Application Administrator to join the OIT Departmental Systems team. This position will be filled at either the Senior Application Administrator (Grade 10) or Lead Application Administrator (Grade 11) level, depending on the finalist's depth of qualifications, technical expertise, and relevant experience. Senior Application Administrator (Grade 10) This position directly supports the technology needs of IT applications across a wide range of divisions and departments, including but not limited to Dining Services, Campus Life, Auxiliary services (Bookstore, Mailroom, Transportation), the Brown Card Office, and the Brown Arts Institute.  This position is responsible to ensure that IT applications meet the ongoing needs of all operational aspects in their respective areas.  The Senior Application Administrator will support all computing applications used throughout our broad customer base.  The Senior Application Administrator will support all of these applications in a variety of ways, including application configuration, vendor technical support, contractual support, and performing Data Security Reviews.  The Senior Application Administrator will participate in and support all upgrades, application and security patches, etc. and will coordinate all aspects of testing, documentation, and training of end users.  The position will participate in cross training with fellow team members to ensure the team has adequate backup for all applications supported. The Senior Application Administrator will be a liaison into OIT, working with the ITSC team, Network and Comm Ops teams, ISG, and any other teams as needed.  This role will also partner with Athletics leaderships regarding technology planning, budgeting, and evaluation of new applications. Education and Experience    ● Bachelor’s degree preferred  ● 3+ years of IT related experience including enterprise-level business application support or administration. The following experience is preferred:  ○   Administration of Public Safety or Enterprise Applications & Systems  ○ Security Systems Application Administration  ○ SQL Queries; including writing queries and joining databases  ○ SSRS (SQL Server Reporting Services); writing reports & supporting SSRS  ○ Active Directory Security Group Administration  ○ Group Policy Administration  ● Lead experience preferred  The following application support or administration experience or equivalent is preferred: ○ Software House - CCURE9000  ○ VMS Systems such as Genetec Security Center  ○ Central Square IMC  ○ NICE 911 Recording Suite  ○ Zetron Communication Solution  ○ SQL Server Reporting Services  ○ Wowza Media Service & TheoPlayer Cloud  The following certifications preferred:  ○ Software House - CCURE9000 Certified  ○ Genetec - Genetec Security Center Certified  ● Strong application support/administration abilities to troubleshoot, support, and maintain critical application suites/software components supporting a 24x7 operation.  ● Strong problem solving skills, organizational skills, and project planning skills  ● Working knowledge of databases and SQL Queries  ● Troubleshooting skills for problem resolution  ● Knowledge of TCP/IP networking  ● Knowledge of IT change management processes  ● Excellent customer service skills; strong commitment to customer service  ● Strong computing, analytical, and organizational skills  ● Ability to work effectively in a group and as a member of a project team  ● Excellent coordination, collaboration, writing, and verbal communication skills  ● Ability to manage multiple tasks with shifting priorities  ● Ability to work through problems and find solutions  ● Experience with Google Suite  ● Experience with Microsoft Excel, Word and other Microsoft Office applications  ● Higher education experience preferred      Lead Application Administrator, Departmental Systems (Grade 11) This position directly supports the technology needs of the customer base for Departmental Systems.  It will primarily focus on the Division of Athletics and the Department of Public Safety and Emergency Management, but will help to support the various other departments and divisions supported by Departmental Systems.   The Lead Application Administrator will support all computing applications used throughout our customer base.   This position will support software apps used by Athletics including enterprise level apps like TeamWorks, that includes NCAA compliance management, University Ticketing for selling tickets to sporting events, and Fusion for managing recreational sports.  Additionally this position supports many sport-specific applications with unique needs.  The Lead Application Administrator will support all of these applications in a variety of ways, including application configuration, vendor technical support, hardware needs except for PCI related equipment, contractual support, and performing Data Security Reviews.  The Lead Application Administrator will participate in and support all upgrades, application and security patches, etc. and will coordinate all aspects of testing, documentation, and training of end users.  The position will participate in cross training with fellow team members to ensure the team has adequate backup for all applications supported. The Lead Application Administrator will be a liaison into OIT, working with many OIT teams including ITSCs, Network, Comm Ops, ISG, Systems, and any other teams as needed.  This role will also partner with customer leadership regarding technology planning, budgeting, and evaluation of new applications. Education and Experience  Bachelor’s degree preferred  7 years of IT related experience  Experience with enterprise-level business application support or administration preferred ​ The following experience is preferred:  SQL Queries; including writing queries and joining databases  Active Directory Security Group Administration  Group Policy Administration ​ The following application support or administration experience or equivalent is preferred:  Athletics enterprise apps; Athletics compliance, Recreational sports management, ticket sales applications Strong application support/administration abilities to troubleshoot, support, and maintain critical application suites/software components supporting a 24x7 operation.  Strong problem solving skills, organizational skills, and project planning skills  Working knowledge of databases and SQL Queries  Troubleshooting skills for problem resolution  Knowledge of TCP/IP networking  Knowledge of IT change management processes  Excellent customer service skills; strong commitment to customer service  Strong computing, analytical, and organizational skills  Ability to work effectively in a group and as a member of a project team  Excellent coordination, collaboration, writing, and verbal communication skills  Ability to manage multiple tasks with shifting priorities  Ability to work through problems and find solutions  Experience with Google Suite  Experience with Microsoft Excel, Word and other Microsoft Office applications  Higher education experience preferred ​ A successful completion of a criminal background check and education verification is required. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-27 Job Posting Title: Senior /Lead Application Administrator, Departmental Systems Department: Office of Information Technology Grade: Grade 11 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Waterman-Street-118-120/Laboratory-Safety-Specialist_REQ210828": {
      "title": "Laboratory Safety Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: Position Purpose The Laboratory Safety Specialist for the Department of Environmental Health & Safety provides support to faculty, students, and staff to help facilitate, assess, and promote a safe and healthy working environment in research laboratories and research support spaces.   The major responsibilities for this position will be to support the laboratory safety program by providing training, conducting inspections, assessing ventilation equipment, and providing risk assessments of lab related work. This position will help with other safety and compliance related projects as needed.  In addition, this position is part of the Emergency Response Team required to respond to emergencies as a rotating member of the emergency on-call team before, during, and after business hours including weekends and holidays on a rotating schedule.    Job Qualifications B.S. in Biology or related science or A.S. in Biology A minimum of 3 years of experience working in a research laboratory, safety department, or doing environmental compliance or the equivalent combination of education and experience. Must be able to obtain IATA and DOT hazardous materials shipping certifications. Job Competencies Capable of obtaining medical clearances for using respiratory protection necessary for HAZMAT response. Good interpersonal skills. Good presentation and public speaking skills. Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds to shoulder height. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background check and pre-employment screenings satisfactory to Brown University. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-08-13 Job Posting Title: Laboratory Safety Specialist Department: Facilities Management and Campus Operations Grade: Grade 9 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location:   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
