    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/South-Street-Landing/Director-of-Business-Development--Health-and-Biomedical-Innovation_REQ210548": {
      "title": "Director of Business Development, Health and Biomedical Innovation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: About Brown  Brown University is a leading research university distinct for its student-centered learning and deep sense of purpose. Our students, faculty and staff are driven by the idea that their work will have an impact in the world. Brown University offers a flexible work/life balance; summer hours, winter break and a comprehensive Benefits package including time off, annual paid holidays; benefits offerings including health, dental, vision, tuition assistance, retirement, wellness, employee discounts and more.  To learn about Brown University’s benefits, visit the University Human Resources web page for further information. About the Opportunity Brown Technology Innovations is a team of dedicated professionals committed to fostering an entrepreneurial culture within the health and biomedical sectors at Brown University, Brown University Health, and Care New England. Under this cooperative, upcoming new investments in technology transfer initiatives will help health system-based researchers turn their discoveries into real-world applications for patients.  Reporting to the Senior Director of Business Development – Life Sciences, the Director will play an integral role in supporting these new initiatives to integrate and align innovation efforts across all three parties. In this role, the Director serves two key stakeholder groups: Faculty and staff inventors responsible for creating innovative technologies. Industry partners—including investors, entrepreneurs, and companies—focused on commercializing those technologies. Major responsibilities include: Technology evaluation & intellectual property management Deal sourcing, negotiations & execution The Director must demonstrate expertise in technology evaluation, intellectual property (IP) protection, and the sourcing, negotiation, and execution of transactions across life sciences fields such as therapeutics, diagnostics, and health information technology. Education and Experience Advanced degree required (MD and/or PhD preferred) Ideally, a minimum 10 years of experience in academic research, business development, innovation management, or technology commercialization. Experience working with or within academic medical centers is a plus. Job Competencies Strong aptitude in patent prosecution and a genuine interest in early-stage technologies and emerging markets. Advanced written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills to convey complex technical, legal, and financial concepts. Deep understanding of licensing structures, valuation models, and negotiation strategies for IP and sponsored research agreements. Well-developed network of investors, entrepreneurs, and business development professionals in the life sciences sector. Ability to work independently, analyze complex policy issues, and follow through with minimal oversight. Proven ability to engage effectively with diverse internal and external constituencies across all organizational levels. While this role is hybrid, there is an expectation that the Director will be in-person a minimum of 2-3 days per week. Additional Information  Applicants are asked to include a resume and cover letter with their application.  All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown University. This is a hybrid position and the employee will be expected to be on campus 3-4 days/week. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-29 Job Posting Title: Director of Business Development, Health and Biomedical Innovation Department: Brown Technology Innovations Grade: Grade 13 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/South-Street-Landing/Intellectual-Property-Technology-Specialist_REQ210466": {
      "title": "Intellectual Property Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: About Brown  Brown University is a leading research university distinct for its student-centered learning and deep sense of purpose. Our students, faculty and staff are driven by the idea that their work will have an impact in the world. Brown University offers a flexible work/life balance; summer hours, winter break and a comprehensive Benefits package including time off, annual paid holidays; benefits offerings including health, dental, vision, tuition assistance, retirement, wellness, employee discounts and more.  To learn about Brown University’s benefits, visit the University Human Resources web page for further information. About the Opportunity Reporting to the Associate Director, Licensing Compliance and Royalty Distribution, this role serves as a strategic subject matter expert, providing critical guidance and technical insights to Business Development Directors regarding the university’s patent portfolio. Assisting in the management of a  diverse portfolio of 500+ active patent families, the incumbent is responsible for the full lifecycle of intellectual property assets. The incumbent will leverage advanced technical expertise and a deep understanding of 35 U.S.C. 2011 Edition statutes to oversee the filing, prosecution, maintenance, and defense strategies required to support commercialization goals. This role acts as a vital bridge between faculty inventors and outside counsel, ensuring that patent strategies are not only legally sound but also commercially optimized. By conducting in-depth IP analysis and quality oversight, this position ensures that the university’s intellectual capital is robustly protected and positioned for successful licensing and institutional impact . Responsibilities include: Portfolio Management & Strategic Planning Operations & Quality Control Stakeholder Engagement & Administration Education and Experience Required Bachelor’s degree required; an advanced degree (Master’s or PhD) in a scientific or technical field is preferred. 3-5 years of experience supporting an IP portfolio within an academic, tech transfer, corporate or related environment or an equivalent combination of education and related experience Work experience within a technology licensing office at a major university is a plus.    Registered Patent Agent status is a plus. Job Competencies Working knowledge of patent prosecution (35 U.S.C. 2011 Edition). Detailed understanding of the nuanced issues related to the protection and enforcement of IP within an academic or research institution. Superior verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to translate complex IP concepts for a variety of stakeholders. Proven ability to manage a large, complex workload, prioritize tasks, and juggle multiple projects in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency in Excel and computer databases to create ad hoc reports for data analyses. High degree of professionalism, diplomacy, and collaboration. Demonstrated maturity in navigating the needs of multiple stakeholders within a complex academic environment. Excellent analytical and decision-making skills, with the ability to exercise good judgment and discretion independently. Demonstrated ability to interact effectively and productively with faculty and senior officials from academia, industry and government. Additional Information  Applicants are asked to include a resume and cover letter with their application.  As this is a hybrid position, the employee would be expected to be on campus a few days per week. All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown University. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-23 Job Posting Title: Intellectual Property Technology Specialist Department: Brown Technology Innovations Grade: Grade 10 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/2-Stimson-Avenue/Administrative-Coordinator_REQ210255-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: The Administrative Coordinator provides operations support to the Swearer Center community of students, staff, faculty and community partners. Reporting to the Center’s Senior Director of Community Engagement , the position supports Swearer Center programs and daily operations by processing financial transactions, supporting event planning, and planning logistics for Swearer staff and student travel. This position plans and executes center-wide annual events and monthly programming-related events by the Swearer Center. The position will serve as a liaison with relevant internal Brown offices (e.g., Financial Operations of the Office of Financial Strategy & Planning, Event Operations, Office of Information Technology, Facilities Management, etc.), and external constituents (e.g., guest speakers and vendors). The position supports building maintenance, inventory and supply ordering, provides front-desk reception, and works as a member of the operations staff to maintain and improve the Center’s operational processes. The position also provides operational support to the Office of Community Engagement. The ideal candidate is responsive, solution-oriented, detail-oriented, resourceful, organized, proactive, and committed to social justice. This is a full-time position. Qualifications Education and Experience Required: Bachelor’s degree with 1-2 years of related experience or equivalent combination of education/experience. Preferred: Administrative experience in an academic or higher education setting preferred. Experience processing financial transactions (reimbursements, purchase orders, etc.) preferred. Experience with event planning preferred. Experience with calendar management or executive support preferred.  Job Competencies Excellent organizational, administrative, and time-management skills and strong attention to detail. Ability to efficiently manage multiple tasks with competing priorities. Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team. Ability to take initiative and prioritize in a fast-paced environment while anticipating emerging needs of the organization. Strong solution and system orientation. Excellent interpersonal/communication skills. Ability to interact professionally with multiple audiences and people from diverse backgrounds. Excellent technical skills in word processing, spreadsheet/database and email applications (Google environment including mail, calendar, drive); experience with project management systems (e.g, Basecamp) and other IT or financial systems (e.g., Workday) preferred. Ability to handle confidential or sensitive materials with discretion. Ability to work nights and weekends and other flexible hours, as needed. Flexibility to handle emergency needs. Additional Information Applicants are asked to include a resume and cover letter. The priority application deadline for this position is August 14, 2026. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of a background check. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-09 Job Posting Title: Administrative Coordinator Department: Howard R. Swearer Center for Public Service Grade: Grade 8 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
    },
    "https://brown.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/South-Street-Landing/Assistant-Director-of-Business-Development_REQ210465": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Business Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description: About Brown Brown University is a leading research university distinct for its student-centered learning and deep sense of purpose. Our students, faculty and staff are driven by the idea that their work will have an impact in the world. Brown University offers a flexible work/life balance; summer hours, winter break and a comprehensive Benefits package including time off, annual paid holidays; benefits offerings including health, dental, vision, tuition assistance, retirement, wellness, employee discounts and more.  To learn about Brown University’s benefits, visit the University Human Resources web page here for further information. About the Opportunity Reporting to the Senior Director of Business Development, Life Sciences, the Assistant  Director (AD) of Business Development serves as a key operational lead in advancing Brown University’s mission to commercialize internal technologies. The AD is responsible for the hands-on management of a complex portfolio of life science technologies. The AD independently performs complex work requiring significant judgment to identify key barriers to commercialization and apply advanced knowledge to resolve them. This role is not merely supportive but is accountable for ensuring that specific goals, objectives, and all work within their assigned pipeline are accomplished. Core Responsibilities include: Technology Sourcing and Discovery: Proactively engages with the research community to identify and evaluate emerging technologies and high-potential inventions. Faculty Business Partnership: Acts as a dedicated consultant to faculty and researchers, providing strategic guidance on commercialization pathways. IP Portfolio Management and Prosecution: Oversees the end-to-end IP filing and prosecution process, including managing relationships with external patent counsel, reviewing legal filings for technical accuracy, and ensuring that the patent strategy aligns with the broader commercialization roadmap Strategic Portfolio Prioritization: Evaluates commercialization opportunities within assigned portfolio to maximize impact Marketing, Outreach and Deal Execution: Identifies and cultivates relationships with potential licensees, industry partners, and venture capitalists to drive engagement and awareness.  Negotiate agreements that protect the institution’s interests while fostering innovation. Job Qualifications Education and Experience Education: Bachelor’s degree in a relevant technical field (Life Science or Biomedical Engineering, etc.) required. An advanced degree (Ph.D., Master’s, MBA, or JD) is preferred. Experience: Minimum of 5 years of related experience in academic research, business development or technology commercialization. Experience working in or with academic institutions and/or medical centers is a plus.   Job Competencies Knowledge: Experience with the practices and processes related to technology transfer and intellectual property. Problem Solving: Ability to resolve a wide range of complex, multi-stakeholder issues in creative ways and work collaboratively to make decisions in ambiguous situations. Collaboration: Proven ability to work cross-functionally across departments and influence others to reach agreement. Communication: Advanced written and verbal communication skills to convey technical and financial data to diverse constituencies. This role is hybrid with an expectation of a minimum of 2-3 days per week in the office Additional Information  Applicants are asked to include a resume and cover letter with their application.  As this is a hybrid role, the employee will be expected to be in the office 3-4 days/week. All offers of employment are contingent upon a criminal background check and education verification satisfactory to Brown University. Benefits of Working at Brown: Please review additional information on the Benefits of Working at Brown . Recruiting Start Date: 2026-07-23 Job Posting Title: Assistant Director of Business Development Department: Brown Technology Innovations Grade: Grade 11 Worker Type: Employee Worker Sub-Type : Regular Time Type: Full time Scheduled Weekly Hours: 37.5 Position Work Location: Hybrid   Submission Guidelines: The designated Position Work Location for each position determines the approved modality of work. Positions are classified based on the operational and business needs of the department and may be designated as on-site, hybrid, or remote. Employees with a designated position work location as remote must reside and perform their work in a state where Brown University is registered to do business. Brown University is a registered employer in the following states: Rhode Island, California, Colorado, Connecticut, Florida, Maryland, Massachusetts, New York, New Hampshire, New Jersey, North Carolina, Washington, D.C. Please note that to be considered for a staff position at Brown University, you must submit a separate application for each position you wish to be considered for. Applications are reviewed only for the specific position to which they are submitted and are not automatically considered for future openings.   This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Still Have Questions? If you have any questions you may contact employment@brown.edu . Brown is an E-Verify Employer. EEO Statement: Brown University provides equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination, harassment and retaliation based upon a person’s race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or any other characteristic protected under applicable law, in the administration of its policies, programs, and activities. The University recognizes and rewards individuals on the basis of qualifications and performance. The University maintains certain affirmative action programs in compliance with applicable law."
